<!DOCTYPE qhelp SYSTEM "qhelp.dtd">
<qhelp>
  <overview>
    <p>
      Triggers such as <code>pull_request_target</code> and
      <code>workflow_run</code> can run with trusted repository context while
      processing data influenced by less-trusted events.
    </p>
  </overview>
  <recommendation>
    <p>
      Split untrusted event processing from write operations. Use read-only
      token permissions for the event-handling job, and move repository writes
      to a separate protected workflow or a narrowly scoped job that does not
      checkout or execute untrusted code.
    </p>
    <p>
      Repository-specific exceptions are limited to the pinned CLA assistant
      with fixed signature storage and no checkout or run step, and the
      upstream-only Python publication jobs whose complete conditions require
      <code>github.repository == 'openai/codex'</code>. The Python exception
      only records that those jobs cannot run in this Sedna fork; it is not an
      assessment of canonical OpenAI publisher or reusable-build safety. Do not
      generalize either exception without preserving its exact gate.
    </p>
  </recommendation>
</qhelp>
